[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a bounded change: it adds filtering to the one existing page, [38;5;153mpublic/activity.html[39m, and touches no other code.
  I'll put a short design here in chat rather than write a spec, and I won't change any code until you approve it.

  Where the filters go is easier to judge by looking, so I've opened three wireframes in a browser tab:
  [94m]8;id=svsvov;http://localhost:51155/?key=fed6cb981411de51a3d892284c046a08ae8bca9c3d701c42cec9837e00c173a1\http://localhost:51155/?key=fed6cb981411de51a3d892284c046a08ae8bca9c3d701c42cec9837e00c173a1[39m]8;;\

  The companion saves its files under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo, so that folder should go in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m. I haven't
  changed [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m. The wireframes use rough placeholder styling, not the token system.

  - [1mA. Filter bar above the table.[0m It has an event type select, a date range, and a search over device, location and IP.
    A live count below it reads "Showing X of 48 events". Every control is always visible.
  - [1mB. A's bar, plus tags and a shortcut.[0m Each active filter also shows as a removable tag. A "Show failed sign-ins"
    button sets that filter in one click, since every support ticket so far was about a failed sign-in. It adds a bit
    more markup and testing than A.
  - [1mC. A "Filter" button that opens a panel.[0m The page header stays quiet, but the controls are hidden, so people may not
    notice they can filter. That works against the original complaint.

  I recommend B. It is A plus one shortcut, and that shortcut covers the failed sign-in case behind every ticket so far.

  Two other questions come after this one, because they affect review. First, the table is empty when JavaScript is off,
  which breaks the NOTES.md rule. Second, the repo has no shared token sheet, and [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m already uses raw hex and
  px values.

  Which layout do you want? You can click one in the browser or answer here.

